    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] FK Partizan is a professional football club based in Belgrade, Serbia.\n[2] The 1966 European Cup Final was a football match held at the Heysel Stadium, Brussels, on 11 May 1966 that saw Real Madrid of Spain defeat Partizan of Yugoslavia 2–1.\n[3] Its local rival Partizan Belgrade was the first Southeast and Eastern European football club to reach the European Champions Cup final, when it did so in 1966.\n[4] They also became the first Eastern European club to play in the European Cup final, losing by Real Madrid in 1966."
